        "thought_text": "Thought-2 (replaced): Instead of simulating the balance year-by-year inside the binary search loop, precompute the balance iteratively once up to the point where it exceeds $10^{18}$ and store the results in a list, then use binary search or direct lookup on this precomputed array to find the answer in $O(\\log(\\text{max\\_years}))$ time, avoiding the $O(N)$ simulation per check that causes the timeout.",
